WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.012 --> 00:00:15.979
Rose sat by the boy's bed and smoothed his hair away from his face.

2
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.681
As she bent over him, her tears fell upon his forehead.

3
00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:22.523
The boy stirred and smiled in his sleep.

4
00:00:22.543 --> 00:00:26.285
"This poor child couldn't have been the pupil of robbers!"

5
00:00:26.705 --> 00:00:27.426
exclaimed Mrs.

6
00:00:27.486 --> 00:00:29.146
Maylie. Dr.

7
00:00:29.166 --> 00:00:30.007
Losberne sighed.

8
00:00:30.027 --> 00:00:31.568
"It's possible."

9
00:00:32.568 --> 00:00:33.868
"But at so early an age?"

10
00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:34.989
Rose protested.

11
00:00:36.089 --> 00:00:37.609
The doctor mournfully shook his head.

12
00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:40.990
"Crime, like death, is not confined to the old."

13
00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:46.332
"But even if he has been wicked, he may never have known a mother's love or the comfort

14
00:00:46.372 --> 00:00:47.752
of a home," said Rose.

15
00:00:47.772 --> 00:00:52.033
"Hunger may have driven him to live with evil men who turned him to crime."

16
00:00:52.994 --> 00:00:53.894
Then she turned to Mrs.

17
00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:58.675
Maylie. "Dear aunt, think what might have become of me if you hadn't taken me in.

18
00:00:59.776 --> 00:01:00.816
Oh, have pity on him!"

19
00:01:02.592 --> 00:01:03.813
Mrs. Maylie hugged Rose.

20
00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:06.294
"Do you think I would harm him?

21
00:01:07.255 --> 00:01:08.716
What can I do to save him, Dr.

22
00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:12.378
Losberne?" "The boy will soon wake," said the doctor.

23
00:01:12.398 --> 00:01:15.160
"I propose that I question him in front of you.

24
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.241
If he's truly bad, he shall be left to his fate.

25
00:01:19.142 --> 00:01:21.123
But if he's good, I'll intervene for him."

26
00:01:22.224 --> 00:01:24.485
Oliver was very ill and weak from loss of blood.

27
00:01:25.406 --> 00:01:29.308
Yet he managed to tell the sad story of his life, and everyone was moved by it.

28
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.582
Rose's gentle hands smoothed Oliver's pillow.

29
00:01:33.503 --> 00:01:35.905
He felt calm and happy as he fell back to sleep.

30
00:01:37.046 --> 00:01:38.707
Dr. Losberne went down to the kitchen.

31
00:01:39.648 --> 00:01:40.229
He found Mr.

32
00:01:40.249 --> 00:01:44.412
Giles and Brittles entertaining the servants and the policeman again with the story of the robbery.

33
00:01:44.432 --> 00:01:46.614
"How is the patient, sir?"

34
00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:47.435
asked Mr.

35
00:01:47.475 --> 00:01:50.798
Giles. "So-so," replied the doctor.

36
00:01:50.818 --> 00:01:55.181
"Can you and Brittles swear that the boy upstairs is the boy who was put through the window

37
00:01:55.221 --> 00:01:55.682
last night?

38
00:01:56.623 --> 00:01:57.884
Come on, out with it!"

39
00:01:59.616 --> 00:02:04.099
The doctor, who was normally quite kind and patient, made this demand in a dreadful tone of anger.

40
00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.661
Giles and Brittles stared at each other.

41
00:02:06.681 --> 00:02:10.083
"Pay great attention to their reply," Dr.

42
00:02:10.103 --> 00:02:11.765
Losberne said sharply to the policeman.

43
00:02:11.785 --> 00:02:14.106
"It's a simple question of identity."

44
00:02:14.126 --> 00:02:17.669
"That's what it is indeed, sir," replied the policeman.

45
00:02:17.689 --> 00:02:20.831
"A house is broken into," said Dr.

46
00:02:20.851 --> 00:02:24.794
Losberne. "A couple of men catch a glimpse of a boy in the darkness.

47
00:02:26.014 --> 00:02:27.856
The next morning a boy comes to the house.

48
00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:32.230
And because he has his arm bandaged, they grab him and swear he is the thief."

49
00:02:33.491 --> 00:02:34.772
The policeman nodded wisely.

50
00:02:34.792 --> 00:02:38.034
"I ask you again," thundered the doctor.

51
00:02:38.054 --> 00:02:42.137
"Are you, on your solemn oaths, able to identify that boy?"

52
00:02:43.238 --> 00:02:44.519
Brittles looked doubtfully at Mr.

53
00:02:44.559 --> 00:02:45.439
Giles, and Mr.

54
00:02:45.479 --> 00:02:46.880
Giles looked doubtfully at Brittles.

55
00:02:48.662 --> 00:02:51.884
The policeman put his hand behind his ear the better to hear the reply.

56
00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:57.588
The two female servants leaned forward And just then there was a knock at the front door.

57
00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.960
"It's the detectives from London!"

58
00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.941
cried Brittles, appearing much relieved.

59
00:03:01.961 --> 00:03:03.621
"The what?"

60
00:03:04.021 --> 00:03:04.802
exclaimed the doctor.

61
00:03:04.822 --> 00:03:07.622
"The London detectives, sir," said Brittles.

62
00:03:07.642 --> 00:03:09.803
"We sent for them this morning."

63
00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.324
Brittles went upstairs and opened the door.

64
00:03:13.244 --> 00:03:14.244
Two men stood there.

65
00:03:15.405 --> 00:03:18.245
One was stout with black hair, and the other was thin with red hair.

66
00:03:19.206 --> 00:03:20.486
Brittles led them into the parlor.

67
00:03:20.506 --> 00:03:25.887
"Tell your master that Blathers and Duff are here," said the stout man, laying a pair of handcuffs

68
00:03:25.927 --> 00:03:26.388
on a table.

69
00:03:27.852 --> 00:03:28.773
"Oh! Good evening, master.

70
00:03:29.593 --> 00:03:31.094
Can I have a word with you in private?"

71
00:03:32.775 --> 00:03:36.498
Blathers addressed this remark to the doctor, who had entered the parlor with the two ladies.

72
00:03:37.438 --> 00:03:38.959
Dr. Losberne dismissed Brittles.

73
00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.162
"This is the lady of the house," said Dr.

74
00:03:42.202 --> 00:03:43.543
Losberne, motioning toward Mrs.

75
00:03:43.603 --> 00:03:47.385
Maylie. Then he proceeded to tell the story of the attempted robbery.

76
00:03:47.405 --> 00:03:53.209
"I can't say for certain until I've examined the evidence," said Blathers, "but I don't think this was

77
00:03:53.249 --> 00:03:54.250
done by local people."

78
00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.212
"Certainly not," said Duff.

79
00:03:58.348 --> 00:04:00.489
"Who is this boy that the servants are talking about?"

80
00:04:00.889 --> 00:04:01.569
asked Blathers.

81
00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:06.130
"One of the frightened servants took it into his head that the boy had something to do with

82
00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:06.670
the robbery.

83
00:04:07.491 --> 00:04:10.051
But it's nonsense, sheer absurdity," said Dr.

84
00:04:10.091 --> 00:04:12.832
Losberne. "Where did this boy come from?

85
00:04:13.772 --> 00:04:15.413
He didn't drop out of the clouds, did he?"

86
00:04:15.773 --> 00:04:16.393
asked Blathers.

87
00:04:16.413 --> 00:04:21.734
"Of course not," replied the doctor with a nervous glance at the two ladies.

88
00:04:21.754 --> 00:04:27.036
"I know his whole history, but first wouldn't you like to see where the thieves made their attempt?"

89
00:04:28.124 --> 00:04:29.665
"Certainly," replied Blathers.

90
00:04:29.685 --> 00:04:33.526
"We should inspect the premises first and examine the servants afterward.

91
00:04:34.386 --> 00:04:35.926
That's the usual way of doing business."

92
00:04:37.127 --> 00:04:41.448
So everyone went off to examine the little window, where the thieves had gained entry to the house.

93
00:04:42.788 --> 00:04:48.230
Then while the detectives interviewed the servants in the kitchen, the doctor paced the parlor in an uneasy

94
00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.970
state. Mrs.

95
00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.411
Maylie and Rose looked on with anxious faces.

96
00:04:52.431 --> 00:04:55.292
"I hardly know what to do," said Dr.

97
00:04:56.876 --> 00:05:00.838
Losberne. "Surely the poor child's story will be enough to show he's innocent," said Rose.

98
00:05:00.858 --> 00:05:03.680
"I doubt it, my dear," said Dr.

99
00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:08.822
Losberne. "He admits that he has been the companion of thieves for quite some time.

100
00:05:09.783 --> 00:05:11.484
He was arrested on a pickpocket charge.

101
00:05:12.404 --> 00:05:17.827
Violent men brought him here to rob the house "Oh, why did the servants send for the detectives?"

102
00:05:18.268 --> 00:05:18.848
cried Rose.

103
00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:22.890
"We cannot let these men know the boy's real story," Dr.

104
00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:23.891
Losberne said firmly.

105
00:05:25.031 --> 00:05:26.312
The detectives soon returned.

106
00:05:27.264 --> 00:05:31.527
Blathers announced that the robbers were probably two men from the city, who used a boy to climb

107
00:05:31.547 --> 00:05:32.167
through the window.

108
00:05:33.288 --> 00:05:34.829
He insisted on seeing Oliver.

109
00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:36.870
Holding a candle, Mr.

110
00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:39.672
Giles led the detectives upstairs to Oliver's bedside.

111
00:05:40.613 --> 00:05:42.694
Dr. Losberne followed with Rose and Mrs.

112
00:05:42.754 --> 00:05:46.397
Maylie. "This lad was wounded by a trap meant for poachers."

113
00:05:47.337 --> 00:05:49.339
Dr. Losberne helped Oliver to sit up in bed.

114
00:05:49.359 --> 00:05:53.321
"He was trespassing near here and came to the house for help this morning.

115
00:05:54.202 --> 00:05:57.064
Mr. Giles immediately grabbed him and put the boy's life in danger.

116
00:05:57.964 --> 00:05:59.044
Do you deny that, Giles?"

117
00:05:59.064 --> 00:06:02.285
"It was all done for the best, sir."

118
00:06:03.246 --> 00:06:04.526
Mr. Giles was bewildered.

119
00:06:05.486 --> 00:06:06.927
"I thought it was the robbers' boy."

120
00:06:06.947 --> 00:06:09.567
"Well, do you think so now?"

121
00:06:09.987 --> 00:06:10.608
asked Blathers.

122
00:06:10.628 --> 00:06:12.528
"I don't know.

123
00:06:12.548 --> 00:06:14.429
I really don't know."

124
00:06:15.329 --> 00:06:16.489
Mr. Giles shook his head.

125
00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:18.610
"I couldn't swear it's him."

126
00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.951
"You're a muddle-headed chap," said Duff.

127
00:06:23.051 --> 00:06:26.880
Dr. Losberne suggested they ask the same question of Brittles.

128
00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.522
But Brittles was no more certain of the boy's identity than Mr.

129
00:06:29.562 --> 00:06:30.303
Giles had been.

130
00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:33.385
"It could be the same boy," said Brittles.

131
00:06:33.405 --> 00:06:35.127
"But it might not be.

132
00:06:36.007 --> 00:06:37.709
I only thought it was the same boy because Mr.

133
00:06:37.729 --> 00:06:38.629
Giles said it was."

134
00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.912
At last Blathers shook his head in disgust.

135
00:06:41.932 --> 00:06:45.235
"There is no robber here," he pronounced.
